hermes v0.22.5: a profile whose config.yaml carries the stock
`model.base_url: https://api.anthropic.com` sends its Anthropic credential
to api.anthropic.com even when the environment points that credential at
a gateway (ANTHROPIC_TOKEN + ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, e.g. TeamClaude).

Symptom: every turn of such a profile fails with `HTTP 401: OAuth access
token is invalid`: Anthropic rejects the gateway's client key. Profiles
without a base_url line in config.yaml work. hermes' model picker writes
that line whenever anthropic is chosen
(hermes_cli/model_setup_flows_common.py), so any profile set up through
it is affected.

Cause: hermes_cli/runtime_provider.py _anthropic_cfg_base_url() returns
config.yaml's model.base_url for provider anthropic, and every native
Anthropic runtime path prefers it to everything else: the credential-pool
row (_pool_entry_mode_and_url; the env:ANTHROPIC_TOKEN row carries
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL but loses to the config), the env runtime
(_anthropic_env_runtime, which ignores ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL altogether) and
--api-key (_explicit_anthropic). The auxiliary client (_try_anthropic)
applies the same config override. Three side call sites never look at
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL and send the token to api.anthropic.com regardless:
the model picker's live catalog (_anthropic_catalog), `hermes doctor`
(_probe_anthropic) and the OAuth usage read (_fetch_anthropic_account_usage,
`/usage`).

Fix: agent/anthropic_credentials.py gains is_stock_anthropic_base_url()
(https + api.anthropic.com, optional :443, `/v1` and trailing slash),
anthropic_env_base_url() (ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL through the secret scope, so
a multiplexed profile reads its own .env) and
effective_anthropic_base_url(): an empty or stock configured base_url
yields to ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL when that is set; any other configured
endpoint (another proxy) still wins. _anthropic_cfg_base_url() and the
auxiliary client's config override go through it; the env runtime and
--api-key fall back to ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL before api.anthropic.com; the
catalog and doctor query ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL; the OAuth usage read reports
"unavailable" instead of sending a token routed through a non-Anthropic
endpoint (the runtime base_url, else ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL) to Anthropic's
usage endpoint. Without ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL nothing changes.

Upstream status: not reported upstream; main (c2f14e48b8, 2026-10-31)
still prefers the config base_url and ignores ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL there.

The regression tests fail before this change: the stock base_url (or none,
for the env and --api-key paths) beats ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL on every
runtime path, the auxiliary client, catalog and doctor, and the usage
read calls api.anthropic.com with the gateway token.

